36a2dd027) - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors (2400x1350 @ 60.00 Hz, 1920x1080 @ 60.00 Hz) - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2070 (NVIDIA; 32.0.16.1088) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-10750H CPU @ 2.60GHz (12 threads) - 15.82 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nMentioned here https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122802#pullrequestreview-5021379645\n\nWhen 2D is floating, selecting a 2D node switches from 3D to the next main screen.\n\nWhen 3D is floating, selecting a 2D node hides the 3D editor content, leaving a blank window and selecting a 3D node again doesn't fix it.\n\nThe steps are so similar that I suspect they are caused by the same issue, something with the 3D editor not wanting to be shown.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nFloating 2D editor:\n\n1. Make the 2D editor floating (leave all others as default).\n2. Have 2D and 3D nodes in the scene.\n3. Open the 3D editor.\n4. Select a 3D node.\n5. Select a 2D node.\n6. The main screen switches to the next dock (Script), it shouldn't.\n\nFloating 3D editor:\n\n1. Make the 3D editor floating (leave all others as default).\n2. Have 2D and 3D nodes in the scene.\n3. Open the 2D editor.\n4. Select a 3D node.\n5. Select a 2D node.\n6. The 3D editor content is hidden.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.c